<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>app.curant.irisinbox</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <!-- Homebrew python3.12, NOT /usr/bin/python3 (Apple's system
             Python) , same reasoning as every other scheduled plist
             in this directory: this run's subprocess.run(["curant-cli",
             "iris-inbox-check"]) call needs curant-cli on PATH, and this
             process's own Automation permissions (if it ever needs
             them for anything downstream) are tied to the exact
             requesting binary, which only the Homebrew python has been
             granted. -->
        <string>/opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.12/bin/python3.12</string>
        <string>-u</string>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/curant-watcher.py</string>
        <string>--iris-inbox-check</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Runs every hour (3600 seconds) rather than a fixed clock time ,
         unlike the daily briefing, there's no reason to wait for a
         specific hour to check an inbox for something that might need
         a reply. This job never messages the customer directly (see
         run_iris_inbox_check's docstring) , it only reads and queues
         drafts into pending_email_sends, which the next daily briefing
         (com.curant.dailybriefing.plist) surfaces and asks the customer
         to approve/reject. Adjust StartInterval if hourly is too
         frequent or not frequent enough for how busy the connected
         inbox actually is. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>3600</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- launchd does not source .zshrc/.zprofile, so curant-cli
         (installed to this Mac's personal ~/bin) is not found on the
         default PATH without this , same fix already applied to every
         other scheduled plist here. -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/AbhyudayDhundhel/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <!-- Dev/testing bypass, matching every other plist here.
             Remove once a real license is activated via curant-cli
             activate. -->
        <key>CURANT_DEV_UNLICENSED</key>
        <string>1</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-irisinbox.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-irisinbox-error.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Install with:
  cp com.curant.irisinbox.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.irisinbox.plist

Before loading, connect the inbox this job should watch:
  curant-cli mcp-add iris-gmail npx -y @shinzolabs/gmail-mcp
(or use a different connection name and point this job at it with
curant-cli set-iris-inbox NAME , default is "iris-gmail").

This job can only READ and DRAFT (queue_email_for_approval) , it has
no ability to actually send, delete, or modify anything in the real
inbox. Sending only ever happens after a live customer approves a
queued draft in a real conversation (see process_email_approvals in
curant-cli). Review what's pending anytime with:
  curant-cli pending-email-sends

To test immediately, run curant-watcher.py directly with the flag shown
in ProgramArguments above, or just run curant-cli iris-inbox-check
directly.

Logs land at /tmp/curant-irisinbox.log and /tmp/curant-irisinbox-error.log.
-->
